ontrol his airborne bloodblades like  homing missiles they are also full of  deadly poison so he's shocked that  tengen hasn't dropped dead at this point  we find out another strength of tangents  because he's from a ninja family he's  actually developed some resistance to  poison it's also revealed that tengan  grew up in a family where his father  forced him to train intensely and he was  one of only two of his nine siblings who  survived tangent goes on to hold his own  against gyutaro and daki until the three  demon-slaying amigos arrive but it's  significant that the poison though not  killing him yet is working slow and  steady and so we gotta keep in mind that  this fight will include tangent far from  prime condition and i say that while  also noting that he failed to kill the  two demons before he was heavily  poisoned as well another significant  detail that's revealed over the course  of the fight is that gyutaro has already  eaten 15 pillars and daki has eaten  seven so right away if tangent comes out  of this alive it's impressive in and of  itself then the battle resumes and  yutaro goes after tanjiro but tundra is  saved by tengen's speed and pulled to  safety tundra admits that he was holding  tengen back by forcing the ladder to  protect him tundra soon repays the favor  though and while tangent thinks it's too  late to avoid some blood blades tundra  manages to use some water breathing to  deflect the attacks they work together  and even a wife of tangents helps by  launching kunai at yutaro at this point  tangent has an amazing moment where he  gets close to utero and even with kunai  hitting him he maintains his focus and  thanks to his ninja training doesn't  even flinch from the multiple kunai hits  he manages to distract yutaro dodge an  attack of his and then akunai hits a  distracted yutaro while tangent cuts the  demon's legs it was an amazingly  executed combo since the kunai was laced  with wisteria flowers gyutaro doesn't  regenerate right away his body goes numb  however the upper moon is too powerful  and a poison that would affect an  unnumbered demon for half a day stops  affecting yutaro pretty soon as his leg  regenerates in this way he catches  tundra and tangent off guard but tengen  has the ability to kick tundra to safety  before he dies he also uses sound breath  forth form death nails of avicii to  block yutaro's countless blood blades  yutaro though takes tengan's wife  hostage and as he does tangent gets a  flashback of her saying and i quote once  we defeat an upper moon let's retreat  from the front lines end quote so  clearly retirement is something that was  on tangent's mind even before this fight  thanks to his wives tundra ends up being  the one to save her to giutaro's  surprise even a combined attack though  doesn't stop yutaro in fact he even  manages to rescue doki's head from  inosuke by stabbing him with his  poisoned sickle in the meantime tanjiro  sees that tangen is on the ground  seemingly down for the count after the  last attack he suffered from giutaro  even one of his arms is cut off so  things look really bad and like the many  pillars who fell to gyutaro before him  it seems like tengen has lost not only  is he this hurt he's also been poisoned  for quite some time at this point and  gyutaro seems to believe that he's even  dead yutaro ends up telling tanjo that  tengen was weak and determination was  his only strength thinking that the  pillar was down for the count however  after tundra takes up some of yootaro's  time and ends up being in trouble tengen  suddenly appears and comes to the rescue  holding one of his blades in his mouth  zoro style it turns out gyutero was  wrong tengen wasn't dead he actually  forced his own heart to stop to keep the  poison from circulating this not only  let him survive for longer it also  opened the possibility for this surprise  attack we're told and this builds off  the music and sound theme that  accompanies tangent that tangent has  analyzed combat maneuvers to the point  where he can read them like sheets of  music it just takes time he converts the  rhythm of the enemy's attacks into sound  so every fight becomes a song he hears  repeated phrases and can attack between  beats and during the rests dancing with  his opponent but the poison has him at  his limit so he can't deliver the final  blow that's pretty cool to know about  tengen and so in general he would do  better in prolonged fights because he  has a better sense of the opponent's  rhythms but in this case the poison has  complicated things and tundra has to be  the one to finish gyutaro off  nonetheless tengen is very impressive  and now that he has a grasp on his  opponent's rhythm he manages to deflect  most of his attacks with one arm to give  to the shock  does end up slicing through one of  tengen's eyes and again tengen is such a  boss it doesn't even slow him down now  that i think about it that's another  thing he has in common with zoro not  making a big deal out of insanely  painful injuries eventually thanks to  tengen's help tundra manages to cut off  kyotaro's head as zaito and enosuke do  the same with daki which is the key for  beating these two so they stop  regenerating yutaro's body unleashes one  more surprise an explosion of blood  blades antagonist prackly at death's  door when the dust settles his tongue  stops working from the poison and he  looks horrible but luckily nezuko's  flames succeed in curing him of the  poison he lost an eye and an arm but  he's alive unlike the other pillars who  face gyutaro albeit he did have a lot of  help from tanjiro nezuko inosuke zenitsu  and his wives during chapter 97 there's  also a pretty hilarious bittersweet  moment when tangent and his wives look  exhausted and unimpressed saying six  that's the lowest of the upper ranks and  quote it's obviously good that they beat  an upper moon but also disheartening at  the same time because it was so hard and  they took so much damage just to beat  the weakest upper moon this realization  probably plays a role in tangan's  decision to retire although even before  the actual fight there was mention of  retiring when they beat an upper moon  anyways it's just lucky in this case  that they ended up confronting 6 rather  than akaza or someone stronger sun emmy  the snake pillar doesn't help matters  when he shows up and says and i quote  what are you going to do about losing  your hand and eye in a fight with mere  upper six end quote clearly among the  pillars tangent's feat wasn't as  impressive as we might have thought it  was and tangent knows this and even says  his plan is to retire and that there's  no way he can fight anymore he does tell  the angered tsunami though that tundra  and the others have grown strong so  they'll be able to make up for his loss  there's no doubt about it tengen was  amazing and he did as well as he could  he was brave cool and pretty strong so i  want to give him full props however it's  clear that among the pillars as he  himself acknowledges he's no genius some  people might think i'm hitting on him in  the comments but it's not an insult to  his character you can be a weaker  character and still be an awesome  character and among the current  generation of pillars tangent is among  the weaker ones as we know gyoume is the  strongest and muichiro the other pillar  tangent singled out as being especially  talented beat upper moon 5 by himself  without losing an arm or eye at only 14  years old while tangent got as hurt as  he did from upper moon 6 a weaker upper  moon while he also had a lot of help to  boot it seems this generation of pillars  is especially talented though since as  we mentioned upper moon 6 beat many  pillars from the past but i'd say he  wouldn't have fared so well against this  generation and tengen said as much when  he said that gyutaro was lucky if he  thought that tangent was especially  talented because that meant he  co